  "domain": "infer-distributed",
  "level": "L2",
  "title": "An async RPC wrapper does not supply inference cancellation or transactional cache rollback",
  "mechanism": "At this TGI revision, Prefill and Decode call model.generate_token synchronously inside async RPC methods. Decode calls cache.pop for each input batch before concatenation/generation and caches the successor only afterward; the wrapper contains no rollback across those operations. SIGINT/SIGTERM change a cooperative flag polled by serve_inner, which has no explicit server.stop or drain call in this unit.",
  "corrections": [
    "A missing later batch causes the handler to raise after earlier pop calls. Actual cache removal and recovery semantics depend on the Cache implementation, which was not included; do not assert a measured lost batch.",
    "Event-loop blocking and transport-level cancellation remain structural inferences, not observed runtime traces.",
    "Cache-delete/clear API calls alone do not prove physical device-memory release.",
    "Use distinct Prefill:151-191 and Decode:193-226 references when stating absence of a handler-local cancellation check."
  ],
  "source_scope": "All 11 corrected references read from pinned Git; no server process or grpc runtime test run.",
